\par
\fs32 Experiment 1: Vector and Matrix Operations for Deep Learning\par
\b0\fs22 1. \b Aim\b0\par
To perform vector and matrix operations using NumPy, calculate cosine similarity between customers, implement a dense neural network layer and visualise recommendation scores using a heatmap.\par
\b 2. Algorithm\par
\b0 1. Import NumPy and Matplotlib.\par
2. Create customer\f1\endash genre and genre\endash book matrices.\par
3. Perform dot product, matrix multiplication and transpose.\par
4. Calculate inverse and element-wise operations.\par
5. Calculate cosine similarity between customers.\par
6. Identify the two most similar customers.\par
7. Calculate dense layer output using \\(y=Wx+b\\).\par
8. Plot the score matrix as a heatmap.\par
3. Program\par
\b\f0\lang1033 Code\f1\lang9\par
\b0 import numpy as np\par
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\par
\par
C = np.array([\par
    [5,4,0,2,1],\par
    [4,5,1,0,2],\par
    [1,2,5,4,0],\par
    [0,1,4,5,3],\par
    [5,3,1,2,4],\par
    [1,0,4,3,5]\par
])\par
\par
G = np.array([\par
    [1,0,2,1],\par
    [2,1,0,1],\par
    [0,2,1,0],\par
    [1,1,2,1],\par
    [2,0,1,2]\par
])\par
\par
scores = C @ G\par
\par
print("Matrix Product:\\n", scores)\par
print("Transpose:\\n", C.T)\par
\par
A = np.array([[2,1],[1,2]])\par
print("Inverse:\\n", np.linalg.inv(A))\par
\par
print("Element-wise Addition:\\n", C+2)\par
print("Element-wise Multiplication:\\n", C*2)\par
\par
norm = np.linalg.norm(C, axis=1)\par
sim = C @ C.T / np.outer(norm,norm)\par
\par
print("Cosine Similarity:\\n", sim)\par
\par
sim[np.diag_indices(6)] = -1\par
i,j = np.unravel_index(np.argmax(sim),sim.shape)\par
print("Similar Customers:",i+1,j+1)\par
\par
W = np.array([[1,2,1,0,1],\par
              [0,1,2,1,1]])\par
b = np.array([1,2])\par
\par
y = W @ C[0] + b\par
print("Dense Output:",y)\par
\par
plt.imshow(scores,cmap="viridis")\par
plt.colorbar()\par
plt.xlabel("Books")\par
plt.ylabel("Customers")\par
plt.title("Recommendation Score Heatmap")\par
plt.show()\par
\par
\par
\b 4. Input\par
\b0 - Customer\endash genre matrix: 6 \f0\'d7 5.\par
- Genre\f1\endash book matrix: 5 \f0\'d7 4.\par
- Weight matrix and bias vector for the dense layer.\par
\par
