\b\fs32 Experiment 2: Cosine Similarity\par
\fs22 Aim\b0 : To calculate cosine similarity between two customer vectors.\par
\par
\b Algorithm:\par
\b0 1. Import NumPy.\par
2. Define two customer vectors.\par
3. Calculate dot product and vector magnitudes.\par
4. Find cosine similarity and display the result.\par
\b Code\b0 :\par
import numpy as np\par
\par
A = np.array([5,4,0,2,1])\par
B = np.array([4,5,1,0,2])\par
\par
s = np.dot(A,B)/(np.linalg.norm(A)*np.linalg.norm(B))\par
print("Cosine Similarity:", round(s,4))\par
\par
\b Input\b0 :\par
A = [5, 4, 0, 2, 1]\par
B = [4, 5, 1, 0, 2] \par
\par
\par
\b Output:\par
\b0 Cosine Similarity: 0.9130\par
\par
\par
\b Result\b0 : Thus, the cosine similarity between the two customer vectors was calculated as 0.9130, indicating high similarity.\par
