\b\fs28 Experiment 4: Entropy and KL Divergence\par
\fs22 Aim\b0 : To calculate entropy, cross-entropy and KL divergence between two probability distributions.\par
\par
\b Algorithm\b0 :\par
1. Import NumPy.\par
2. Define probability distributions P and Q.\par
3. Calculate entropy.\par
4. Calculate cross-entropy and KL divergence.\par
5. Display the results.\par
\b Code\b0 :\par
import numpy as np\par
\par
P = np.array([0.5, 0.3, 0.2])\par
Q = np.array([0.6, 0.25, 0.15])\par
\par
H = -np.sum(P * np.log2(P))\par
CE = -np.sum(P * np.log2(Q))\par
KL = np.sum(P * np.log2(P / Q))\par
\par
print("Entropy:", round(H, 4))\par
print("Cross Entropy:", round(CE, 4))\par
print("KL Divergence:", round(KL, 4))\par
