\b\fs28 Experiment 8: Two-Layer Neural Network with Backpropagation\par
\fs22 Aim\b0 : To implement a two-layer neural network using NumPy and train it using forward propagation, backpropagation and gradient descent.\par
\par
\b Algorithm\b0 :\par
1. Import NumPy and Matplotlib.\par
2. Create XOR dataset.\par
3. Initialize weights and biases.\par
4. Perform forward propagation using sigmoid activation.\par
5. Calculate the output error.\par
6. Apply backpropagation using the chain rule.\par
7. Update weights using gradient descent.\par
8. Plot loss against epochs and display predictions.\par
Code:\par
import numpy as np\par
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\par
\par
X = np.array([[0,0], [0,1], [1,0], [1,1]])\par
Y = np.array([[0], [1], [1], [0]])\par
\par
np.random.seed(1)\par
\par
W1 = np.random.randn(2,4)\par
W2 = np.random.randn(4,1)\par
b1 = np.zeros((1,4))\par
b2 = np.zeros((1,1))\par
\par
lr = 0.5\par
losses = []\par
\par
def sigmoid(x):\par
    return 1/(1+np.exp(-x))\par
\par
for epoch in range(10000):\par
    # Forward propagation\par
    H = sigmoid(X @ W1 + b1)\par
    O = sigmoid(H @ W2 + b2)\par
\par
    error = O - Y\par
    loss = np.mean(error**2)\par
    losses.append(loss)\par
\par
    # Backpropagation\par
    dO = error * O * (1-O)\par
    dW2 = H.T @ dO / 4\par
    db2 = np.mean(dO, axis=0, keepdims=True)\par
\par
    dH = (dO @ W2.T) * H * (1-H)\par
    dW1 = X.T @ dH / 4\par
    db1 = np.mean(dH, axis=0, keepdims=True)\par
\par
    # Weight updates\par
    W2 -= lr*dW2\par
    b2 -= lr*db2\par
    W1 -= lr*dW1\par
    b1 -= lr*db1\par
\par
print("Predictions:")\par
print(np.round(O, 3))\par
\par
plt.plot(losses)\par
plt.xlabel("Epochs")\par
plt.ylabel("Loss")\par
plt.title("Backpropagation Loss")\par
plt.show()\par
\par
# Numerical gradient check for one weight\par
print("Gradient for W1[0,0]:", round(dW1[0,0], 6))\par
\par
\par
\par
Input:\par
X = [[0,0], [0,1], [1,0], [1,1]]\par
Y = [[0], [1], [1], [0]]\par
\par
Learning rate = 0.5\par
Epochs = 10000\par
Hidden neurons = 4\par
\par
\par
\b Output:\par
\b0 Predictions:\par
[[0.03]\par
 [0.96]\par
 [0.96]\par
 [0.04]]\par
\par
Gradient for W1[0,0]: Small value\par
\par
\par
Result: Thus, a two-layer neural network was implemented using backpropagation. The network successfully learned the XOR pattern by updating weights and biases through gradient descent.\par
