\b\fs32 Experiment 10: L2, Dropout and Early Stopping Comparison\par
\fs22 Aim\b0 : To compare L2 regularization, Dropout and Early Stopping techniques to reduce overfitting in a neural network.\par
\par
\b Algorithm\b0 :\par
1. Import NumPy, TensorFlow and Matplotlib.\par
2. Generate a sample diabetes dataset.\par
3. Split the dataset into training and testing sets.\par
4. Train a baseline neural network.\par
5. Apply L2 regularization with different values.\par
6. Apply Dropout with different rates.\par
7. Apply Early Stopping.\par
8. Compare training accuracy and testing accuracy.\par
\b Code\b0 :\par
import numpy as np\par
import tensorflow as tf\par
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\par
from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\par
\par
np.random.seed(42)\par
\par
# Sample diabetes dataset\par
X = np.random.rand(500, 8)\par
y = (X[:,0] + X[:,1] + X[:,2] > 1.5).astype(int)\par
\par
X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\par
    X, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\par
\par
def create_model(l2=0, drop=0):\par
    model = tf.keras.Sequential([\par
        tf.keras.layers.Input(shape=(8,)),\par
        tf.keras.layers.Dense(64, activation='relu',\par
            kernel_regularizer=tf.keras.regularizers.l2(l2)),\par
        tf.keras.layers.Dropout(drop),\par
        tf.keras.layers.Dense(32, activation='relu'),\par
        tf.keras.layers.Dense(1, activation='sigmoid')\par
    ])\par
    model.compile(optimizer='adam',\par
        loss='binary_crossentropy', metrics=['accuracy'])\par
    return model\par
\par
results = []\par
\par
# Different regularization methods\par
settings = [\par
    ("Baseline", 0, 0),\par
    ("L2 0.01", 0.01, 0),\par
    ("Dropout 0.2", 0, 0.2),\par
    ("Dropout 0.5", 0, 0.5)\par
]\par
\par
for name, l2, drop in settings:\par
    model = create_model(l2, drop)\par
    model.fit(X_train, y_train, epochs=30, verbose=0)\par
\par
    train_acc = model.evaluate(X_train, y_train, verbose=0)[1]\par
    test_acc = model.evaluate(X_test, y_test, verbose=0)[1]\par
\par
    results.append([name, train_acc, test_acc])\par
\par
# Early stopping\par
model = create_model()\par
early = tf.keras.callbacks.EarlyStopping(\par
    monitor='val_loss', patience=3, restore_best_weights=True)\par
\par
model.fit(X_train, y_train, validation_split=0.2,\par
          epochs=30, callbacks=[early], verbose=0)\par
\par
train_acc = model.evaluate(X_train, y_train, verbose=0)[1]\par
test_acc = model.evaluate(X_test, y_test, verbose=0)[1]\par
results.append(["Early Stopping", train_acc, test_acc])\par
\par
# Display comparison\par
print("Model | Train Accuracy | Test Accuracy")\par
for r in results:\par
    print(r[0], round(r[1], 3), round(r[2], 3))\par
\par
plt.bar([r[0] for r in results],\par
        [r[2] for r in results])\par
plt.xticks(rotation=30)\par
plt.ylabel("Test Accuracy")\par
plt.title("Regularization Comparison")\par
plt.show()\par
\par
\par
\b Input\b0 :\par
- Dataset size: 500 records.\par
- Features: 8 clinical features.\par
- Target: Diabetes (0 = No, 1 = Yes).\par
- L2 values: 0.01.\par
- Dropout rates: 0.2 and 0.5.\par
- Epochs: 30.\par
